Embedded web fonts (SVG output)
-------------------------------

  assets/fontembed/*.woff2, assets/fontembed/*.css
  (compiled in with the `font-embed` cargo feature)

  The woff2 files are the ones mermaid-cli embeds into the SVGs it writes,
  unchanged: @fontsource-variable/recursive@5.3.0 and @fontsource/open-sans@5.3.0
  (SIL Open Font License 1.1, see above) and the web fonts of
  @fortawesome/fontawesome-free@7.3.1 (SIL Open Font License 1.1 with the
  Reserved Font Name "Font Awesome"; the CSS carries the package's licence
  text, as mermaid-cli writes it). The CSS files are those packages'
  stylesheets as mermaid-cli serialises them, each with its licence comment,
  and a placeholder where the font's data URL goes (tools/gen_font_embed.py).
  Every embedded sheet carries the licence text, as the OFL requires.
